meta {
  name: ServiceOwnerDelegationRequests
  seq: 4
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  # Delegation requests: generic service owner endpoint

  BDD scenarios for the generic service owner delegation request endpoints under
  `/accessmanagement/api/v1/serviceowner/delegationrequests`. They double as usage
  documentation: every request carries a `docs` block with what the endpoint does, the
  parameters it takes, the token and scope it needs, and the response it returns.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a
  known state, removes what it created, and can run standalone or repeatedly.

  ## Endpoints

  - `GET delegationrequests/_meta/urns/party`: the party URN prefixes `from` and `to`
    accept. Anonymous.
  - `POST delegationrequests`: a service owner asks a party to grant another party a
    resource or an access package. Exactly one of `resource` or `package` is set. Scope
    `altinn:serviceowner/delegationrequests.write`, behind the feature flags
    `AccessMgmt.Controller.RequestAssignment.Resource` and `.Package`.
  - `GET delegationrequests/{id}/status` and `PUT delegationrequests/{id}/withdraw`: the
    service owner reads the status of its request and withdraws it again. Scopes
    `altinn:serviceowner/delegationrequests.read` and `.write`.

  The package and resource specific variants are covered by the flat folders
  `AccPkg_DelegationRequest` and `Resource_DelegationRequest`.

  ## Tokens and fixtures

  Every step mints a Maskinporten enterprise token for ttd through `helpers.js`
  (`loginAsServiceOwner(serviceOwner, scope)`); ttd owns the requested resource. The
  service owners come from `testdata/sharedtestdata.js`. The personas, resource and
  package come from `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<env>.js`, which picks them
  from the existing testdata files instead of copying their ids.

  ## Environments

  Written for and verified on AT22. There is no seed file for other environments yet.
}
